<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chihuahua (city)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1709">1709</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chihuahua is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, capital of the state of the same name. It was founded in 1709 as a mining settlement after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> was found nearby, and became the chief town of the northern frontier, linked by the Camino Real to Santa Fe and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-hidalgo-y-costilla">Miguel Hidalgo</a> was executed there in 1811, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pancho-villa">Pancho Villa</a> had his headquarters there during the Mexican Revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chihuahua-city.jpg" alt="Chihuahua (city)" width="320" height="588" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: El Sombrerero · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chihuahua_montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
